# Copy to services/catalog/.env for anything other than the default.
# The file is read by src/env.ts through process.loadEnvFile, and a variable
# already present in the environment always wins, so CI and one-off overrides
# such as `DATABASE_URL=... npm run catalog -- status` are never shadowed.
#
# .gitignore already covers .env* except .env.example. Never commit a real one.

# The catalog database. This default is the Homebrew Postgres 17 install with a
# database created by `createdb self_learn`, which is what daily development
# runs against — no container, no password, no configuration.
#
# CI and the homeserver run the postgres:17 container in compose.yaml instead:
#   DATABASE_URL=postgres://catalog:catalog@localhost:5432/self_learn
DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5432/self_learn

# The two submodule checkouts. Both default to where .gitmodules puts them, so
# neither needs setting; they exist because that location has changed once
# already (the pair moved from the repo root into tools/ on 2026-09-13) and
# because a checkout kept outside the superproject is a reasonable thing to
# have. A relative value resolves against the repo root, not the working
# directory, and a leading ~ is expanded.
#
# MANIMKC_ROOT is manimkc's own variable and means the same thing here: the
# *checkout*, which `catalog index` reads and runs the pinned CLI out of.
# `--manimkc-root` overrides it for one run. It is NOT MANIMKC_HOME, which is
# where manimkc's renders land; the indexers take that from each report's
# `outRoot` and never from a path set here.
# MANIMKC_ROOT=tools/manimkc

# TLDRAWKC_ROOT is the tldrawkc checkout, whose dist/ build reads the .tldr
# files. `npm run canvas` in the root package.json reads the same variable, so
# the tool and the indexer cannot end up on different builds.
# TLDRAWKC_ROOT=tools/tldrawkc

# The knowledge base's repo root: the directory holding learn/. A test-fixture
# override, not a deployment setting. `learn-cli.test.ts` points it at a
# throwaway tree (with DATABASE_URL at a scratch database) so a test run cannot
# touch the real learn/ or the real self_learn. Leave it unset and every learn
# command works against this repo.
# LEARN_ROOT=/tmp/learn-fixture

# Let this process write to a database whose catalog_instance row says `copy`
# (edge case 14 of docs/CONTENT-MIGRATION.md). Every table carries a statement
# trigger that refuses writes on a copy and names the primary; this flag makes
# the connection set `self_learn.copy_ok = on`, which the trigger lets through.
# For the test suites and scripts/e2e.mjs, which write to throwaway copies on
# purpose. Never set it here: a laptop that needs it is pointed at the wrong
# database. `catalog migrate` sets it by itself, since a copy's schema still
# has to follow the primary's.
# CATALOG_COPY_OK=1

# The data root for the laptop's blob store, which keeps objects under
# $SELF_LEARN_HOME/blobs (docs/CONTENT-MIGRATION.md 0.4). Defaults to
# ~/.self-learn, so the store is ~/.self-learn/blobs. Absolute or starting
# with ~/; a relative value is refused rather than resolved against wherever a
# command happens to run. `fsStore` refuses a root inside a self-learn
# checkout. `blobRoot()` in src/env.ts reads it, for the catalog CLI and for
# the web app alike, which is why this file is the place to set it. Tests and
# scratch work point it at a temporary directory.
# SELF_LEARN_HOME=~/.self-learn
